Memtis: guard the toptier-demotion underflow and make the demotion scan preemptible.

need_toptier_demotion() triggers on the demotion watermark (2%, floor 50 MB) but sizes the
demotion with the promotion watermark, whose floor returns MIN_WATERMARK_LOWER_LIMIT (50 MB).
For a fast tier of ~2.44-3.26 GiB the demotion watermark exceeds the promotion watermark, the
unsigned nr_exceeded wraps to ~2^64, and demote_lruvec() spins on empty LRU lists with no
yield: soft lockup in kmigraterd0, RCU stall, kthread_stop() hangs (16 G @ 20%, 2026-11-18).
The guard never fires outside that band, so behavior elsewhere is unchanged.
Apply after memtis.patch and memtis-c6420.patch:  git apply memtis-watermark-underflow.patch

--- a/mm/htmm_migrater.c	2026-11-18 16:21:10.379190150 +0000
+++ b/mm/htmm_migrater.c	2026-11-18 16:21:20.387219619 +0000
@@ -171,6 +171,9 @@
 	    return false;
     }
 
+    /* min_wm can exceed max_wm (fast tier ~2.44-3.26 GiB): nothing to demote, don't underflow */
+    if (nr_lru_pages + nr_need_promoted + fasttier_max_watermark <= max_nr_pages)
+	return false;
     *nr_exceeded = nr_lru_pages + nr_need_promoted + fasttier_max_watermark - max_nr_pages;
     return true;
 }
@@ -560,6 +563,9 @@
 	    nr_to_scan -= (long)scan;
 	    if (nr_reclaimed >= nr_to_reclaim)
 		break;
+	    cond_resched();		/* empty-list steps never reach shrink_page_list()'s yield */
+	    if (kthread_should_stop())	/* let memtis-env teardown stop us */
+		break;
 	}
 
 	if (nr_reclaimed >= nr_to_reclaim)
